WEBVTT

00:04.040 --> 00:04.400
There.

00:04.400 --> 00:09.840
Create insert method is the classical way on how we define and create tables in SQL, where first we

00:09.840 --> 00:15.760
have to go and create the table and define the structure, and after that we insert our data into the

00:15.760 --> 00:20.920
database table where the other method, the CTAs create table as select.

00:20.960 --> 00:27.040
This one can create a new table as well, but this time based on the result of SQL query.

00:27.040 --> 00:28.840
So let's understand what this means.

00:28.880 --> 00:31.240
Okay so now to the first method create insert.

00:31.240 --> 00:32.640
So here we have two steps.

00:32.640 --> 00:37.680
The first step is we have a DDL statements where we use the command create.

00:37.680 --> 00:40.160
So once we execute the first step what's going to happen.

00:40.160 --> 00:44.160
The database engine is going to go and create for us an empty table.

00:44.160 --> 00:47.280
It is a brand new table where we can hold our data.

00:47.280 --> 00:52.080
So with that we have defined the structure of our table but it's still an empty table.

00:52.080 --> 00:56.680
So now in the next step we have to go and insert our data inside this new table.

00:56.680 --> 01:02.680
So our data can come from multiple sources like CSV file or maybe completely from another database where

01:02.680 --> 01:03.920
we are doing migration.

01:04.080 --> 01:09.600
Or maybe you are inserting manually your data, or maybe it come from an application, or you are doing

01:09.800 --> 01:12.360
data migration from one database to another.

01:12.360 --> 01:15.480
So at the end, once you execute insert, what's going to happen?

01:15.720 --> 01:18.840
Your data going to be inserted in this new table.

01:18.840 --> 01:20.960
So in this method we have like two steps.

01:20.960 --> 01:27.220
First we define the structure of the table, and the second step we take care of inserting our data

01:27.220 --> 01:28.140
inside the table.

01:28.180 --> 01:32.140
And now this new table and your data can be persisted permanently.

01:32.180 --> 01:34.820
Now let's check the other method the CTAs.

01:34.860 --> 01:38.180
Here it's only one step where you define a query.

01:38.180 --> 01:40.740
And once you execute this query, what's going to happen?

01:40.980 --> 01:44.580
The database has to retrieve the data from another table.

01:44.580 --> 01:49.220
So it might retrieve data from our new table that we just created using create insert.

01:49.220 --> 01:52.820
So once the query is executed we will get a result.

01:52.820 --> 01:56.900
So now what the database is going to do is going to create a new brand table.

01:56.940 --> 02:02.940
But this time the definition and the data of this new table, it doesn't come from any definition that

02:02.940 --> 02:03.820
we specify.

02:04.180 --> 02:06.860
It comes from the result of the query.

02:06.860 --> 02:12.020
So whatever structure that we have in the results it's going to be reflected in our new table.

02:12.020 --> 02:19.460
So again the definition and the data that we see in this new table comes 1 to 1 from the result of our

02:19.460 --> 02:20.060
query.

02:20.060 --> 02:24.620
So in this type we don't have to define anything or to insert any data.

02:24.620 --> 02:26.380
We are just writing a query.

02:26.380 --> 02:28.780
And the output of this query is going to define the table.

02:28.780 --> 02:34.460
But in this method as you can see it always needs a database table in order to execute the query.

02:34.460 --> 02:38.540
But the create insert method we are creating something from the scratch.

02:38.700 --> 02:44.300
So these are the two different ways on how you create tables in SQL and the differences between them.
